The database column `id` is not set to auto-generate values. Either make the DB column use a sequence/serial/IDENTITY, or make the entity use a sequence generator that matches your DB. Below are two options.

SQL fix (apply in psql or migration) — make `id` generated by a sequence / bigserial:
```sql
-- If creating the table:
CREATE TABLE lifting_exercises (
  id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  sets INTEGER,
  reps INTEGER,
  weight DOUBLE PRECISION
);

-- Or, for an existing table: create sequence, set default, and sync sequence with existing max(id)
CREATE SEQUENCE IF NOT EXISTS lifting_exercises_id_seq;
ALTER TABLE lifting_exercises ALTER COLUMN id SET DEFAULT nextval('lifting_exercises_id_seq');
SELECT setval('lifting_exercises_id_seq', COALESCE((SELECT MAX(id) FROM lifting_exercises),0) + 1, false);
```

Java/entity alternative — ensure the entity and DB sequence agree. Update `backend/src/main/java/dev/jclawlor/FitnessGoals/entity/LiftingExercise.java`:
