Meal works because its `id` field is annotated with `@Id` and `@GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)`, so the database (serial/bigserial or identity column) generates the id and Hibernate doesn't try to insert a null. Your `LiftingExercise` entity is likely missing a generated id mapping, so Hibernate attempts to insert a row with a null `id`.

